# BCH: BTC-Only Files Warning

## ⛔ WARNING: YOU ARE ACCESSING A BTC-ONLY FILE

**If you are working on a BCH (Bitcoin Cash) task, STOP IMMEDIATELY.**

These files contain BTC-specific implementations (PSBT, Descriptor, MuSig2) that are **NOT compatible with BCH**.

## Overview

This rule identifies files that are **BTC-ONLY** and must **NEVER** be used, modified, or referenced when working on BCH (Bitcoin Cash) tasks.

## What BCH Should Use Instead

| BTC Feature | BCH Alternative |
|-------------|-----------------|
| PSBT | Raw Transaction Hex |
| `CreatePSBT()` | `CreateRawTransaction()` |
| `SignPSBTWithKey()` | `SignRawTransactionWithKey()` + SIGHASH_FORKID |
| Descriptor import | `ImportAddress()` / `ImportAddressWithLabel()` |
| MuSig2/Schnorr | Traditional P2SH multisig with ECDSA |
| Bech32/Bech32m addresses | CashAddr format (`q...`, `p...`) |
| Taproot (P2TR) | Not supported - use P2PKH or P2SH |

## BCH Signing Requirements

When signing BCH transactions, you MUST use:

```go
// BCH requires SIGHASH_FORKID (0x40) combined with sighash type
// SIGHASH_ALL (0x01) + SIGHASH_FORKID (0x40) = 0x41

const (
    SigHashAll     = 0x01
    SigHashForkID  = 0x40
    BCHSigHashType = SigHashAll | SigHashForkID  // 0x41
)
```

